  "question": {
    "text": "If the deBroglie wavelength of an electron is equal to $10^{-}$ times the wavelength of a photon of frequency $6 \\times 10^{14}$ $\\mathrm{Hz}$, then the speed of electron is equal to :\r\n\r\n(Speed of light $\\left.=3 \\times 10^{8} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}\\right)$\r\n\r\nPlanck's constant $=6.63 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{~J} . \\mathrm{s}$\r\n\r\nMass of electron $\\left.=9.1 \\times 10^{-31} \\mathrm{~kg}\\right)$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$1.1 \\times 10^{6} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1.7 \\times 10^{6} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1.8 \\times 10^{6} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1.45 \\times 10^{6} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "de-Broglie wavelength,\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\lambda=\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\mathrm{mv}}=10^{-3}\\left(\\frac{3 \\times 10^{8}}{6 \\times 10^{14}}\\right) \\quad\\left[\\because \\lambda=\\frac{\\mathrm{c}}{\\mathrm{v}}\\right]\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\mathrm{v}=\\frac{6.63 \\times 10^{-34} \\times 6 \\times 10^{14}}{9.1 \\times 10^{-31} \\times 3 \\times 10^{5}} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\mathrm{v}=1.45 \\times 10^{6} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$"
  }
}